# PII_WEB_CONCURRENCY=4
#   Default: 4 (was 2 — chosen when the sidecar had 2 uvicorn workers).
#   Worker PROCESSES, not threads (GIL-bound NER). Each loads its own model
#   copy: MEASURED ~640MB per worker (sidecar at 2.57GiB with 4 workers), so
#   budget workers x 640MB against free RAM before raising it. This is the
#   sidecar's MEMORY knob first and a CPU knob second.
#   NOTE when checking it is live: the spawned workers are
#   multiprocessing.spawn children, so they do NOT appear as "uvicorn" in ps.
#   Count /proc/*/comm == python3.11 instead, or you will wrongly conclude the
#   workers never started.
#   SET IT TO MATCH OKF_IMPORT_CONCURRENCY — they are one capacity setting. See
#   the PAIRING RULE at the OKF_IMPORT_CONCURRENCY entry above: import lanes
#   above the sidecar's worker count queue instead of adding throughput.
#   Compose: yes. Ansible: yes (pii_web_concurrency).
# PII_REGION_MAX_CHARS=50000
#   Default: 50000 in the sidecar. Max chars per analyze() call. A single long
#   scan holds the GIL inside native spaCy/thinc code, which starves uvicorn's
#   own supervisor: it SIGKILLs a worker that fails its 5 s liveness ping and
#   respawns it. Measured 2026-10-13 — an 850 KB page killed the worker 8/8
#   before this knob existed and 0/10 after; the same page was split into 18
#   regions. LOWER it on a slower host: a region must stay under ~5 s, which
#   is what stops the supervisor kill. Raise it only when a region measures
#   below that. Smaller regions cost a little throughput, never recall.
#   Used by: pii-service. Compose: yes. Ansible: yes (pii_region_max_chars).

