# OKF_INGEST_MAX_CONCEPTS=1000
#   Default: 1000 (was 200). Max concepts per import batch.
#   USE-CASE DEPENDENT — this is a CAPACITY knob, not a safety limit:
#     pilot / demo repository      a few hundred is plenty
#     department knowledge base    ~1000 (the default)
#     national / crawl-scale base  10,000+ — raise it deliberately
#   Why 200 was wrong: the cap is checked AFTER the document-ceiling split, so
#   the operator's "how many documents did I select" is NOT the number the cap
#   sees. Measured on Bali: 999 documents in, 1112 concepts out (89 split
#   families) — a 200 cap rejects that outright. An operator picking 400
#   documents has no way to predict that oversized pages multiply it to 600+.
#   Raising it is safe because the bounds that actually protect the machine are
#   the per-concept document ceiling (OKF_MAX_CONCEPT_DOC_CHARS) and the lane
#   caps — not this number. At 1000, TOO_MANY_CONCEPTS stays reserved for
#   genuine misconfiguration rather than firing on ordinary large crawls.
#   Compose: yes. Ansible: yes.
# OKF_INGEST_MAX_ZIP_BYTES=268435456
